*** Add File:vault/n8n_vault_agent_pattern.md
+# Vault integration pattern for n8n (recommended)
+
+Overview:
+- Do not store long-lived secrets in n8n. Use Vault to hold API keys (GitHub, Rekor, MLflow, Slack, PagerDuty, JIRA).
+- Use a Vault Agent sidecar or Kubernetes Vault Agent Injector to render secrets into a volume at /vault/secrets/n8n_creds.json.
+
+Example Vault objects to create (operator):
+- secret/data/n8n/github: { token: "..." }
+- secret/data/n8n/rekor: { url: "...", api_key: "..." }
+- secret/data/n8n/slack: { webhook: "..." }
+
+Vault role:
+- Create a Kubernetes auth role (k8s) mapped to the n8n service account with minimum read permission to secret/data/n8n/*.
+
+Agent injector:
+- Use vault-agent injector mutation (or helm chart `vault.hashicorp.com/agent-inject` annotation) to populate /vault/secrets/n8n_creds.json
+- Alternatively, run a small init container that queries Vault using a short-lived Kubernetes service account token.
+
+Security notes:
+- Use OIDC/Kubernetes auth for Vault (no static VAULT_TOKEN).
+- Rotate credentials stored in Vault regularly.
+- Limit who can edit n8n workflows (SSO + RBAC).
+
