*** Add File:docs/runbook_n8n.md
+# n8n Runbook — Aegis automations
+
+Purpose: Operational guidance for running n8n as the automation layer for Aegis (HIL, Gatekeeper remediation, incident forensics, enrollment).
+
+Deploy & configure (summary)
+- Deploy n8n in namespace `n8n` (k8s/n8n manifests). For production, use Helm chart with existing values file (helm/values-n8n.yaml).
+- Use managed Postgres where possible; secrets live in Vault and are injected via Vault Agent (see vault/n8n_vault_agent_pattern.md).
+- Protect the UI with OIDC/SSO (configure reverse-proxy ingress to enforce auth).
+- Limit who can edit workflows: create n8n editor role and bind to a small automation team.
+
+Backups & restores
+- Backup Postgres daily (dump + S3). Export workflows periodically via UI or API and commit exports to git (encrypted repo or vault-stored).
+- Test restore workflows monthly by restoring Postgres + importing workflows in a sandbox cluster.
+
+Secrets & credentials
+- Never store long‑lived credentials in n8n. Use Vault for Slack, GitHub, Rekor, MLflow, JIRA, PagerDuty.
+- Provide n8n with a single short‑lived Vault‑issued service token or mount secrets via the Vault Agent.
+
+Monitoring & alerts
+- Export n8n metrics (or instrument job failures) to Prometheus. Alert on:
+  - workflow failures > threshold/hour
+  - error rate in HTTP requests to critical integrations (receipt_signer, Rekor)
+  - high queue length or DB errors
+
+Access control & security
+- Restrict ingress to n8n UI to SSO authenticated users only.
+- Validate and review new workflows via code review before import (use workflow export in git as PR artifact).
+- Enable audit logging of workflow edits and runs (n8n stores executions; rotate logs).
+
+Operational playbooks
+- On workflow failure: examine last execution in UI -> check logs -> replay via manual trigger or runbook script -> if integration credential broken, rotate via Vault and re-run import.
+- On suspected compromise: disable n8n ingress, revoke Vault role used by n8n, export workflows for forensics, and restore from backup into sandbox.
+
