+# Demo playbook — CI + n8n HIL approval + receipt_signer + Rekor (end-to-end)
+
+Step 0 — Prereqs
+- n8n deployed and accessible (n8n.aegis.example.com)
+- Vault with secrets for n8n integrations and Vault Agent configured to seed /vault/secrets/n8n_creds.json
+- receipt_signer, Rekor, MLflow and CI configured (example workflows already in repo)
+- CI configured to call n8n webhook to pause promotion and provide `ci_callback_url` to resume
+
+Step 1 — Import workflows
+- Run: tools/n8n/import_workflows.sh http://n8n.aegis.example.com N8N_API_KEY
+
+Step 2 — Trigger from CI
+- CI job posts to: https://n8n.aegis.example.com/webhook/aegis-hil-approval
+- Example payload:
+  {
+    "model_name": "pricing-v2",
+    "evidence_url": "https://artifacts.example.com/dist/evidence.json",
+    "ci_callback_url": "https://ci.example.com/promotion/resume",
+    "mlflow_run_id": "abcd-1234"
+  }
+
+Step 3 — n8n flow (what happens)
+- Webhook receives the request and posts to Slack notifying approvers with an approval link.
+- The flow waits for an approval signal (via separate webhook triggered by Slack button or UI).
+- On approval, n8n calls receipt_signer /sign with the approval metadata -> receipt_signer returns signed attestation.
+- n8n publishes the signed approval to Rekor and updates the evidence bundle (or notifies MLflow).
+- n8n posts back to the CI `ci_callback_url` to resume the promotion job.
+
+Step 4 — CI resumes and deploys
+- The CI promotion step receives the callback and continues; Gatekeeper + pre-load webhook validate the model at deploy time.
+
+Validation & acceptance
+- Confirm Rekor entry exists and matches the signed approval.
+- Check MLflow run has evidence bundle attached (or accessible).
+- Verify model successfully loads and pre-load webhook returns OK.
+
+Security note: ensure webhook endpoints are internal-only or protected via HMAC signature verification. Use Vault-provided secrets to validate inbound webhooks.
+
